{
    "cells": [
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "# Attendance Prediction Models Comparison - PortAventura World\n",
                "\n",
                "This notebook compares multiple forecasting models to predict monthly attendance for **PortAventura World**.\n",
                "Given the small dataset size (approx 40 observations), we focus on robust models suitable for short time series with seasonality.\n",
                "\n",
                "**Models Evaluated:**\n",
                "1.  **Seasonal Naive**: Baseline\n",
                "2.  **SARIMAX**: Classical statistical model with exogenous variables (for COVID)\n",
                "3.  **ETS (Exponential Smoothing)**: Holt-Winters method\n",
                "4.  **Prophet**: Robust to outliers and missing data\n",
                "5.  **Theta**: Simple and often effective benchmark\n",
                "6.  **Ensemble**: Average of top models\n",
                "\n",
                "**Key Handling:**\n",
                "-   **Yearly seasonality** (period=12)\n",
                "-   **COVID period** (Feb 2020 - June 2021) impact analysis"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Install necessary libraries if not present\n",
                "!pip install prophet statsmodels scikit-learn pandas numpy matplotlib seaborn"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Import libraries\n",
                "import pandas as pd\n",
                "import numpy as np\n",
                "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
                "import seaborn as sns\n",
                "from statsmodels.tsa.statespace.sarimax import SARIMAX\n",
                "from statsmodels.tsa.holtwinters import ExponentialSmoothing\n",
                "from statsmodels.tsa.forecasting.theta import ThetaModel\n",
                "from prophet import Prophet\n",
                "from sklearn.metrics import mean_absolute_error, mean_squared_error, mean_absolute_percentage_error\n",
                "import warnings\n",
                "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
                "\n",
                "# Set visualization style\n",
                "sns.set_style(\"whitegrid\")\n",
                "plt.rcParams['figure.figsize'] = (15, 6)\n",
                "plt.rcParams['font.size'] = 10"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 1. Data Loading and Preprocessing"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Load data\n",
                "df = pd.read_csv('final_data/attendance.csv')\n",
                "df['USAGE_DATE'] = pd.to_datetime(df['USAGE_DATE'])\n",
                "portaventura = df[df['FACILITY_NAME'] == 'PortAventura World'].copy()\n",
                "\n",
                "# Aggregate to Monthly\n",
                "portaventura['year_month'] = portaventura['USAGE_DATE'].dt.to_period('M')\n",
                "monthly_data = portaventura.groupby('year_month')['attendance'].sum().reset_index()\n",
                "monthly_data['date'] = monthly_data['year_month'].dt.to_timestamp()\n",
                "monthly_data = monthly_data.set_index('date').sort_index()\n",
                "\n",
                "# Ensure continuous monthly frequency and fill missing values (e.g. park closures) with 0\n",
                "monthly_data = monthly_data.asfreq('MS').fillna(0)\n",
                "\n",
                "# Define COVID period\n",
                "covid_start = '2020-03-01'\n",
                "covid_end = '2021-06-01'\n",
                "\n",
                "# Create exogenous variable for COVID (binary)\n",
                "monthly_data['covid_dummy'] = 0\n",
                "monthly_data.loc[(monthly_data.index >= covid_start) & (monthly_data.index <= covid_end), 'covid_dummy'] = 1\n",
                "\n",
                "# Visualize\n",
                "plt.figure(figsize=(15, 6))\n",
                "plt.plot(monthly_data.index, monthly_data['attendance'], marker='o', label='Actual Attendance')\n",
                "plt.axvspan(pd.to_datetime(covid_start), pd.to_datetime(covid_end), color='red', alpha=0.1, label='COVID Period')\n",
                "plt.title('PortAventura Monthly Attendance')\n",
                "plt.legend()\n",
                "plt.show()\n",
                "\n",
                "monthly_data.tail()"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 2. Train/Test Split\n",
                "Given the small dataset (41 months), we use a small test set of the last 6 months to evaluate forecast performance."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "train_size = len(monthly_data) - 6\n",
                "train = monthly_data.iloc[:train_size]\n",
                "test = monthly_data.iloc[train_size:]\n",
                "\n",
                "print(f\"Train samples: {len(train)}\")\n",
                "print(f\"Test samples: {len(test)}\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 3. Model Implementation & Evaluation\n",
                "\n",
                "We will define a dictionary to store predictions."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "predictions = pd.DataFrame(index=test.index)\n",
                "predictions['Actual'] = test['attendance']\n",
                "\n",
                "def evaluate_model(y_true, y_pred, model_name):\n",
                "    rmse = np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(y_true, y_pred))\n",
                "    mae = mean_absolute_error(y_true, y_pred)\n",
                "    mape = mean_absolute_percentage_error(y_true, y_pred)\n",
                "    print(f\"--- {model_name} ---\")\n",
                "    print(f\"RMSE: {rmse:,.0f}\")\n",
                "    print(f\"MAE: {mae:,.0f}\")\n",
                "    print(f\"MAPE: {mape:.2%}\")\n",
                "    return {'RMSE': rmse, 'MAE': mae, 'MAPE': mape}"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### 3.1 Seasonal Naive (Baseline)\n",
                "Forecasts the value from the same month last year."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Shift by 12 months\n",
                "predictions['S.Naive'] = monthly_data['attendance'].shift(12).iloc[train_size:]\n",
                "\n",
                "# Handle edge case if shift produces NaNs (e.g. if test set is longer than history which is not here)\n",
                "predictions['S.Naive'] = predictions['S.Naive'].fillna(method='bfill') # simple fallback\n",
                "\n",
                "evaluate_model(predictions['Actual'], predictions['S.Naive'], \"Seasonal Naive\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### 3.2 SARIMAX\n",
                "Using (1,1,1)x(1,1,0,12) as a starting point based on seasonality."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "try:\n",
                "    sarima_model = SARIMAX(train['attendance'], \n",
                "                           exog=train['covid_dummy'],\n",
                "                           order=(1, 1, 1), \n",
                "                           seasonal_order=(1, 1, 0, 12),\n",
                "                           enforce_stationarity=False,\n",
                "                           enforce_invertibility=False)\n",
                "    sarima_results = sarima_model.fit(disp=False)\n",
                "    \n",
                "    # Forecast\n",
                "    sarima_pred = sarima_results.get_forecast(steps=len(test), exog=test[['covid_dummy']])\n",
                "    predictions['SARIMAX'] = sarima_pred.predicted_mean\n",
                "    \n",
                "    evaluate_model(predictions['Actual'], predictions['SARIMAX'], \"SARIMAX\")\n",
                "except Exception as e:\n",
                "    print(f\"SARIMAX failed: {e}\")\n",
                "    predictions['SARIMAX'] = np.nan"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### 3.3 Exponential Smoothing (ETS / Holt-Winters)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "try:\n",
                "    # 'add' for trend and seasonality is often good for attendance if amplitude doesn't scale with level\n",
                "    # 'mul' if seasonal swings assume multiplicative growth. We'll try additive first data seems stable-ish level.\n",
                "    ets_model = ExponentialSmoothing(train['attendance'], \n",
                "                                     trend='add', \n",
                "                                     seasonal='add', \n",
                "                                     seasonal_periods=12).fit()\n",
                "    predictions['ETS'] = ets_model.forecast(len(test))\n",
                "    \n",
                "    evaluate_model(predictions['Actual'], predictions['ETS'], \"ETS (Holt-Winters)\")\n",
                "except Exception as e:\n",
                "    print(f\"ETS failed: {e}\")\n",
                "    predictions['ETS'] = np.nan"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### 3.4 Prophet"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Prophet expects columns 'ds' and 'y'\n",
                "prophet_train = train.reset_index()[['date', 'attendance']].rename(columns={'date': 'ds', 'attendance': 'y'})\n",
                "\n",
                "m = Prophet(yearly_seasonality=True, weekly_seasonality=False, daily_seasonality=False)\n",
                "# Add covid as a regressor? Or let Prophet handle it? \n",
                "# Prophet handles outliers well, but COVID is a structural break.\n",
                "# Let's keep it simple first without extra regressors to test robustness, \n",
                "# usually Prophet fits trend changes automatically if changepoints are allowed.\n",
                "\n",
                "m.fit(prophet_train)\n",
                "\n",
                "future = m.make_future_dataframe(periods=len(test), freq='MS')\n",
                "forecast = m.predict(future)\n",
                "\n",
                "predictions['Prophet'] = forecast.iloc[-len(test):]['yhat'].values\n",
                "evaluate_model(predictions['Actual'], predictions['Prophet'], \"Prophet\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### 3.5 Theta Method\n",
                "Uses decomposition to forecast."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "try:\n",
                "    theta_model = ThetaModel(train['attendance'], period=12)\n",
                "    theta_res = theta_model.fit()\n",
                "    predictions['Theta'] = theta_res.forecast(len(test))\n",
                "    \n",
                "    evaluate_model(predictions['Actual'], predictions['Theta'], \"Theta\")\n",
                "except Exception as e:\n",
                "    print(f\"Theta Model failed: {e}\")\n",
                "    predictions['Theta'] = np.nan"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "### 3.6 Ensemble\n",
                "Average of SARIMAX, ETS, Prophet, and Theta."
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "cols_to_average = ['SARIMAX', 'ETS', 'Prophet', 'Theta']\n",
                "cols_available = [c for c in cols_to_average if c in predictions.columns and not predictions[c].isna().any()]\n",
                "predictions['Ensemble'] = predictions[cols_available].mean(axis=1)\n",
                "\n",
                "evaluate_model(predictions['Actual'], predictions['Ensemble'], \"Ensemble\")"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "markdown",
            "metadata": {},
            "source": [
                "## 4. Final Comparison"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "results = []\n",
                "for col in predictions.columns:\n",
                "    if col == 'Actual': continue\n",
                "    \n",
                "    try:\n",
                "        r = evaluate_model(predictions['Actual'], predictions[col], col)\n",
                "        r['Model'] = col\n",
                "        results.append(r)\n",
                "    except:\n",
                "        pass\n",
                "\n",
                "res_df = pd.DataFrame(results).sort_values('MAPE')\n",
                "\n",
                "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
                "sns.barplot(x='MAPE', y='Model', data=res_df, palette='viridis')\n",
                "plt.title('Model Comparison (MAPE)')\n",
                "plt.xlabel('MAPE')\n",
                "plt.tight_layout()\n",
                "plt.show()\n",
                "\n",
                "print(\"Top Models by MAPE:\")\n",
                "display(res_df)"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": [
                "# Plot forecasts\n",
                "plt.figure(figsize=(15, 8))\n",
                "plt.plot(train.index, train['attendance'], label='Train Data', color='black')\n",
                "plt.plot(test.index, test['attendance'], label='Actual Test Data', color='black', linestyle='--', linewidth=2)\n",
                "\n",
                "colors = ['blue', 'green', 'orange', 'purple', 'red']\n",
                "for i, col in enumerate(['SARIMAX', 'ETS', 'Prophet', 'Theta', 'Ensemble']):\n",
                "    if col in predictions.columns:\n",
                "        plt.plot(predictions.index, predictions[col], label=col, alpha=0.7)\n",
                "\n",
                "plt.title('Forecast Models Comparison')\n",
                "plt.legend()\n",
                "plt.show()"
            ]
        },
        {
            "cell_type": "code",
            "execution_count": null,
            "metadata": {},
            "outputs": [],
            "source": []
        }
    ]
}